message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "DPP-Net: A Dynamic Part-Aware Framework for Few-Shot Rapid Enrollment in Cross-Condition Gait Recognition"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of DPP-Net, a dynamic part-aware prototypical
  framework for few-shot cross-condition gait recognition. A part-aware encoder
  decomposes each gait energy image into eight body-region descriptors, and a
  residual-conditioned attention module reweights those regions per query, so
  that new identities are enrolled from a handful of samples with no retraining
  using only 0.685M parameters.
